WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.790
At this point in the course
you've learned about a few

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:06.020
different techniques for
handling images on the web.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.070
For instance,
you can use external files and

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:13.250
just link to them in your html or
you can inline images and

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:16.335
put all the data you need for
an image right there on your page.

00:00:16.335 --> 00:00:21.880
You can use Raster images like this
picture of the star called Electra.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.400
Or you can use Vector images like this
star from the Material Design icon set.

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:32.320
And then of course you can issue images
altogether and use font icons like font

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:36.160
awesome and then use CSS techniques for
styling them.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.490
Funny thing is that any and

00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:42.950
all of these techniques can lead to
pretty much the same result on the page.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.010
The so called, right strategy.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:47.850
Notice the air quotes there,
for including an image,

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:52.390
almost completely depends on the images
place in your app, as a whole.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.320
For the next few quizzes, I want you to
think through some of the scenarios, and

00:00:56.320 --> 00:00:58.510
decide the best course of action.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:00:59.710
Here's the first scenario.

00:00:59.710 --> 00:01:03.030
You're developing a mobile app that
displays an ever changing catalog

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.910
of bikes for sale.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.690
You need an image for
this start right here,

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:11.892
to indicate which bikes have just gone
on sale within the last 24 hours.

00:01:11.892 --> 00:01:14.980
You want to scale the star
image with the rest of the app,

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.190
in order to fit mobile phones and
tablet's proportionally.

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:22.910
So should you use a vector graphic or
a raster graphic and

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:27.260
should you inline the icon or should
you set its source to external file.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:29.910
Think it through and pick the best
answer for both the questions.

